  "architecture_name": "[efficientnet_b0] efficientnet_b0_adapter",
  "architecture_family": "efficientnet_b0",
  "description": "EfficientNet-B0 with ImageNet pretrained weights, 1-channel mel-spectrogram input expanded to 3 channels via conv1x1, resized to 224x224, with dropout=0.3 before the 206-unit sigmoid output head.",
  "reasoning": "As the first experiment, EfficientNet-B0 is a strong baseline for audio spectrogram tasks \u2014 it offers a good balance between capacity and inference speed. Pretrained ImageNet features transfer well to mel-spectrograms and help with the long-tail minority classes. It's small enough (~5.3M params) to run within the 90-minute CPU Kaggle budget while typically outperforming ResNet18 and custom CNNs on this type of task. Starting with the strongest expected baseline lets us calibrate future experiments."
}
